    {
      "source": "6.1: Equivalent Expressions",
      "section": "warmup",
      "modality": "THREE_DISTINCT_EQUIVALENT_EXPRESSIONS_WITH_DISTRIBUTIVITY",
      "answer": "10(2+3)-8*3=10*5-24=50-24=26. Three forms include 10*2+10*3-24, (50-20)-4, 2*13; all exactly26."
    },
    {
      "source": "6.2: Similarity Transformations (Part 1)",
      "section": "two-figures",
      "modality": "FIRST_PARTY_TRIANGLE_AND_HEXAGON_ORDERED_RIGID_AND_DILATION_FULL_VERTEX_MAPS",
      "answer": "Triangle EGH (0,0),(2,0),(0,1), reflect x->-x, dilate2 O, translate(+5,+1) -> target LMN (5,1),(1,1),(5,3). Hexagon ABCDEF (0,0),(2,0),(3,1),(2,2),(0,2),(-1,1), rotate90 CCW, dilate2 O, translate(+5,+1) -> (5,1),(5,5),(3,7),(1,5),(1,1),(3,-1)."
    },
    {
      "source": "6.3: Similarity Transformations (Part 2)",
      "section": "four-figures",
      "modality": "FOUR_INDEPENDENT_PRESCRIBED_COMBINATIONS_WITH_ORDERED_VERTEX_CORRESPONDENCE",
      "answer": "Original P(0,0),Q(2,0),R(0,1). B translate(+3,+1) then reflect y -> (-3,1),(-5,1),(-3,2); C reflect x then dilate2 -> (0,0),(4,0),(0,-2); D rotate90 CCW then reflect y -> (0,0),(0,2),(1,0); E dilate0.5 then translate(+4,+2) ->(4,2),(5,2),(4,2.5). B,D congruent; C,E similar noncongruent."
    },
    {
      "source": "6.4: Methods for Translations and Dilations",
      "section": "method-cards",
      "modality": "TWO_DIFFERENT_FIVE_CARD_PARTNER_SETS_AND_ORAL_COMPARISON_WITH_TEACHER_OBSERVATION",
      "answer": "Original X(0,0),Y(2,0),Z(0,1) to target (3,1),(7,1),(3,3). A chooses A2 dilate2 O then A1 translate(+3,+1). B chooses B1 translate(+3,+1) then B2 dilate2 about (3,1). Both valid; partner sets separated and teacher scores comparison."
    }
  ],
